  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Above normal temperatures and high humidity today.\n\nA cold front currently passing across Western New York will continue \neast across New York State this afternoon and evening. Ahead of the \nfront, this morning heat and humidity have been on the rise \nsupporting temperatures across the Finger Lakes and eastern Lake \nOntario region to warm up into 80s, whereas prefrontal cloud cover \nand now arrival of the cold air from the front is supporting \ntemperatures to fall a few degrees from the mid 70s to the low 70s. \nExpect locations ahead of the front, Rochester eastward may see \ntemperatures warm up a few degrees more before the frontal passages \nknocks conditions cooler.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Scattered showers and thunderstorms are expected \nthis afternoon across the eastern Lake Ontario region.\n\nA mid-level trough over Ontario and western Quebec, will send it's \nassociated surface cold front to continue to track across the \neastern Great Lakes this afternoon. As this front has encountered a \nwarm soupy airmass across the Finger Lakes, a few showers and \nthunderstorms are beginning to develop. Expect activity to increase \nas the front advances further to the east this afternoon.\n\nDue to the timing of the frontal passage, the severe potential \ncontinues to be of a lesser degree, and is limited to the far \neastern Lake Ontario region. Should storms become severe, the main \nhazards will be damaging winds and heavy rain given the PWAT values \nrange between 1.5 to 2.0 inches.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Showers and thunderstorms return Sunday.\n\nThe next potent shortwave trough will round the base of the mid-\nlevel low over northeastern Ontario, passing across the eastern \nGreat Lakes Sunday. Meanwhile at the surface, a surface low will \ndive southeast across the central Great Lakes and into the Ohio \nValley supporting another cold front to pass east across western and \nnorthcentral New York. With the frontal passage, expect showers and \nthunderstorms Sunday.\n\nSimilar to today and as of this forecast iteration, the timing of \nthe frontal passage doen't align with the favorable conditions for \nsevere weather and therefore at this time, if any thunderstorms \ndevelop, severe weather is not expected at this time.",
